world and the situation.

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:35.683
I think there's a lot of power.

00:08:35.683 --> 00:08:36.810
- And really control of that mystery.

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:37.770
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:39.510
- Yeah and she never kind of,

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:41.490
contradicts what people say about her,

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:42.570
because...
- She leans in.

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:44.500
- It only helps kind of,
build this mythology.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:46.390
- Even the bad review
thing, that was so funny,

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:47.907
I was like, she totally, I'm like,

00:08:47.907 --> 00:08:50.240
"I want that filter", like.
(audience laughs)

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.047
- Where like somebody writes
about you and you're like,

00:08:52.047 --> 00:08:53.130
"Well, they're writing about me".

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:53.963
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:08:53.963 --> 00:08:55.430
- They think I'm awesome
enough to write about.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.440
It was just like the most positive outlook

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:59.780
and I was like, "We all need that".

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:00.860
So, what did it feel like though,

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:02.780
the first time that you
saw yourself as Angelyne?

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:05.080
Did it kind of help you
to get more in character?

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:07.140
- Well, it's such a wild transformation,

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:10.650
and the makeup and hair team
and the prosthetics artists

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.573
and everyone who worked on this,

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:16.080
were, I mean, some days
it took three hours,

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.500
Some days it took seven hours

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:18.940
before I would even go to work.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:19.910
- [Kelly] Oh, my gosh.

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.070
- [Emmy] So, it's really, I mean, that's,

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:25.060
I mean, clearly not what,
I'm not blessed enough

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:25.950
to look like that.
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:28.260
But they did that and
I've got to tell you,

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:31.350
I thought it was, the first
time I looked in the mirror

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:33.470
and saw, not myself.

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:34.510
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:36.680
- It was scary at first
because you're so used to like,

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.050
the context of recognizing yourself.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:39.883
- Yeah.

00:09:39.883 --> 00:09:41.090
- [Emmy] And then there was
this incredible liberation

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:44.800
and I felt so empowered in the body.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:45.693
- [Kelly] Oh, that's cool.

00:09:45.693 --> 00:09:48.210
- That if there, yeah,
after like six months of it,

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:51.353
I was like, "Is this
better? Should I do this?"

00:09:51.353 --> 00:09:52.240
(Kelly and audience laugh)
It's very...

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:54.490
- No, that just looked heavy and like,

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:55.760
maybe back surgery in the future.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:56.640
- [Emmy] It was quite heavy.
(Kelly laughs)

00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:00.940
It was quite heavy and she's
a pint size, little thing, so.

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:02.930
- I know, I loved the
performance part though.

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:04.540
I thought that was the coolest like, part.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.317
Like, it was really, really cool.

